== E2 systools:make_script
fakelib absent : {error,systools_make,[{error_reading,{fakelib,{not_found,"fakelib.app"}}}]}
fakelib on ERL_LIBS: {ok,systools_make,[]}
ok  E2 absent -> error value naming the app
ok  E2 absent names fakelib
ok  E2 control: present -> ok
ok  E2 control: present is not an error
== E3 run-time: ensure_all_started of an app whose declared dep is missing
{error,{fakelib,{"no such file or directory","fakelib.app"}}}
ok  E3 a value, naming the missing app's .app file
control (both on ERL_LIBS): {ok,[fakelib,top]}
ok  E3 control: with fakelib present it starts
== E4/E5 erlc accepts a caller of an absent module; xref flags it
erlc: exit=0 out=[]
ok  E5 erlc says nothing
xref (fakelib absent; xref library path set to code_path): {ok,[{{caller,go,0},{fakelib_mod,hello,0}}]}
ok  E4 xref names the undefined call
ok  E4 ... as an undefined call
xref (fakelib on ERL_LIBS; xref library path set to code_path): {ok,[]}
ok  E4 control: with the app on the path xref is clean

